WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:04.203
Gal and I are about to face off
in a game of Box of Lies.

00:00:04.203 --> 00:00:05.371
Here's how it works.

00:00:05.371 --> 00:00:06.873
Upstage are a bunch of boxes

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:09.409
containing objects neither of us
have seen before.

00:00:09.409 --> 00:00:11.277
Taking turns,
we're going to select a box,

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:12.846
open it on our side
of the table,

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:14.347
out of view of the other person.

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:15.881
You remove the object
from the box,

00:00:15.881 --> 00:00:17.416
show it to our
great audience here,

00:00:17.416 --> 00:00:18.651
and then look at your opponent

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:20.586
and tell them
what's in your box.

00:00:20.586 --> 00:00:23.689
They have to guess if you're
lying or telling the truth.

00:00:23.689 --> 00:00:25.324
We'll play three rounds.

00:00:25.324 --> 00:00:26.993
Gal, why don't you pick
the first box?

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:29.262
-Oh, thank you.
How gentleman of you.

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:30.929
-Yes.
-Any idea?

00:00:30.929 --> 00:00:32.965
[ Audience shouting ]

00:00:32.965 --> 00:00:35.168
5.

00:00:35.168 --> 00:00:36.736
-I will get it for you.

00:00:36.736 --> 00:00:38.337
-[ Speaking foreign language ]

00:00:38.337 --> 00:00:41.140
[ Laughs ] Thank you.
-It feels very light.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:43.376
-Hmm.
-So that's a hint.

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:46.145
-Oh, my God.

00:00:46.145 --> 00:00:49.315
This is awesome.

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:52.118
-Hmm.

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:54.454
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.022 --> 00:00:58.724
Hmm. Yes?

00:00:58.724 --> 00:01:02.695
-You know --
-What is in your box?

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:04.530
What was in your box?
-What I'm hiding...

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:06.966
-Yes.
-...in my box...

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:08.468
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.468 --> 00:01:11.971
It moves. You can hear
the sound of the movement.

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:13.139
Can you hear it?

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:15.608
-No.
-The squeak.

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:18.544
-Squeak?
-Like, it sounds like a squeak.

00:01:18.544 --> 00:01:19.845
I don't know if it's a squeak.

00:01:19.845 --> 00:01:21.447
Like, it's an "eeeh!"
Never mind.

00:01:21.447 --> 00:01:23.049
It's --

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:24.417
-What? What?

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:26.919
-It --
-It sounds like a squeak?

00:01:26.919 --> 00:01:28.588
-You're lying.
-It moves. It moves.

00:01:28.588 --> 00:01:30.689
-It moves. Yeah, yeah. Okay,
that one -- That's the truth.

00:01:30.689 --> 00:01:34.961
It's from -- made out of
plastic. It's an animal.

00:01:34.961 --> 00:01:38.531
It's an elephant
made out of plastic.

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:42.334
And it's thing -- trunk.
Trunk? Moves.

00:01:42.334 --> 00:01:43.803
-Yes, trunk.
-Yeah.

00:01:43.803 --> 00:01:47.239
-All right, so it's a plastic
elephant with a moving trunk.

00:01:47.239 --> 00:01:49.375
-Uh-huh.

00:01:54.947 --> 00:01:57.583
I don't see why you
would be lying about that.

00:01:57.583 --> 00:01:59.485
I think you're telling
the truth!

00:01:59.485 --> 00:02:02.088
-You're so wrong! Ha ha!
-What?!

00:02:02.088 --> 00:02:04.057
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:04.057 --> 00:02:06.292
You are the -- Oh, my gosh!

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:07.760
-I told you I would do better...

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.995
-Gosh! Dumb.

00:02:09.995 --> 00:02:13.365
"Cats rule"?
Get this thing out of here.

00:02:13.365 --> 00:02:15.100
All right. Which number?

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:17.236
[ Audience shouting ]

00:02:17.236 --> 00:02:19.639
Here we go. 2. I can't believe
you got me with that.

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:23.008
[ Grunting ]

00:02:23.008 --> 00:02:26.378
-Acting as if it's very heavy.
-Oh, I don't know. Is it?

00:02:26.378 --> 00:02:29.048
-But it seems to be
really light.

00:02:31.517 --> 00:02:33.553
Hmm.

00:02:33.553 --> 00:02:35.588
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.595 --> 00:02:44.764
You don't know
if you should lie about it

00:02:44.764 --> 00:02:46.499
since it's such a good thing...
-Yeah.

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:48.801
-...or you should just
go for it, right?

00:02:51.638 --> 00:02:52.872
Okay.

00:02:52.872 --> 00:02:55.408
-It's a Cabbage Patch doll head.

00:02:55.408 --> 00:02:56.609
-What is that?

00:02:56.609 --> 00:02:58.978
-You don't have that in Israel?
-A Cabbage what?

00:02:58.978 --> 00:03:01.480
-Cabbage Patch dolls.
Cabbage Patch doll.

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:03.416
-What is that?
-Cabbage Patch kids?

00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:05.317
It's, like, a famous doll.
Do you have dolls?

00:03:05.317 --> 00:03:07.486
Did you have dolls growing up?
-Yeah, we have dolls in Israel.

00:03:07.486 --> 00:03:09.255
Just not...
-All right.

00:03:09.255 --> 00:03:13.059
Well, this is a doll head of a
very famous toy here in America.

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:14.894
-Oh, the sweet, cute, little...
-Yes.

00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:16.663
...girly, yeah.
-Yes.

00:03:16.663 --> 00:03:19.431
But this has Cheerios
glued to its head

00:03:19.431 --> 00:03:22.802
made to look like an afro.

00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:24.737
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.338 --> 00:03:28.942
-You're lying.

00:03:32.044 --> 00:03:34.113
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:36.216
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.951 --> 00:03:40.520
-I've never lost.
This is embarrassing.

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:42.688
All right.
Well, what number for you?

00:03:42.688 --> 00:03:43.889
[ Audience shouting ]

00:03:43.889 --> 00:03:46.426
-7.
-7.

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:49.628
I'm being very nice
and gentlemanly.

00:03:49.628 --> 00:03:52.631
[ Grunts ]
-It's not heavy at all.

00:03:52.631 --> 00:03:53.967
You're playing an act --

00:03:53.967 --> 00:03:55.701
-No, I'm very --
I know, but I'm just --

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:57.870
I'm just --
I don't like losing.

00:03:57.870 --> 00:03:59.472
-Oh, wow.

00:03:59.472 --> 00:04:01.574
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.043 --> 00:04:07.046
I don't even know
how to describe this.

00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:09.781
-Hmm. Right now -- Right now
what's going through your head?

00:04:09.781 --> 00:04:12.085
You're thinking of lying,

00:04:12.085 --> 00:04:13.953
you're thinking of
telling the truth.

00:04:13.953 --> 00:04:15.554
It's a very mixed bag right now.

00:04:15.554 --> 00:04:17.490
You're going through a lot
of emotions, and I feel that.

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:19.058
It's a foot.

00:04:19.058 --> 00:04:20.560
-Food?

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:22.161
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.161 --> 00:04:23.862
Like foot? Or food?

00:04:23.862 --> 00:04:25.764
Foot? You said "foot."

00:04:25.764 --> 00:04:27.266
So that means it's --

00:04:27.266 --> 00:04:29.602
Is it a food --
you eat food?

00:04:29.602 --> 00:04:31.837
Or foot with toes?

00:04:31.837 --> 00:04:34.073
-It's a foot.
-Oh, foot. It's a foot.

00:04:34.073 --> 00:04:35.874
Yeah. It's a foot.

00:04:35.874 --> 00:04:37.943
I mean, but this is --
You're charming me now.

00:04:37.943 --> 00:04:39.945
So this is --
This is all part of the thing.

00:04:39.945 --> 00:04:42.749
Oh, this is a good lie.
You just totally gave it up.

00:04:42.749 --> 00:04:44.250
'Cause now you're being
really charming.

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:46.285
-With, um...
-It is a foot.

00:04:46.285 --> 00:04:48.154
-With, like...

00:04:48.154 --> 00:04:49.589
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:49.589 --> 00:04:51.990
[ Laughter ]

00:04:51.990 --> 00:04:53.893
What is it, now?
What is it, now?

00:04:53.893 --> 00:04:57.830
-With, like, small, little
people skiing off the foot.

00:04:57.830 --> 00:04:59.932
[ Laughter ]

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:06.139
-All right. This is a foot --

00:05:06.139 --> 00:05:11.210
It's a foot with small, little
people skiing off the foot.

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:13.279
[ Laughter ]

00:05:13.279 --> 00:05:16.449
-You are really good.
You're a really good actor.

00:05:16.449 --> 00:05:17.750
All right. Gosh.

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:20.186
I don't know if you're lying
or telling the truth.

00:05:20.186 --> 00:05:24.924
It's a foot with people
skiing off the foot.

00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:32.198
I think you lie!

00:05:32.198 --> 00:05:34.433
-I tell the truth!

00:05:34.433 --> 00:05:36.135
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:36.135 --> 00:05:37.370
-I lost!

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:39.805
[ Bell dinging ]

00:05:39.805 --> 00:05:42.008
You are good.

00:05:42.008 --> 00:05:45.410
Congratulations.
You are the winner.

00:05:45.410 --> 00:05:46.946
Now, as the winner...

00:05:46.946 --> 00:05:49.282
♪♪

00:05:49.282 --> 00:05:52.618
-Gal, as the winner of this...
-Yes.

00:05:52.618 --> 00:05:54.186
-...we have
a special prize for you.

00:05:54.186 --> 00:05:56.288
-Yay!
-Our writer Seth Herzog

00:05:56.288 --> 00:05:58.257
is going to come out
and do a tribute to you

00:05:58.257 --> 00:05:59.592
by doing an interpretive dance

00:05:59.592 --> 00:06:01.760
of the original
"Wonder Woman" theme song.

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:03.896
-That would be amazing!
-So here he is.

00:06:03.896 --> 00:06:05.998
-Where is he?
-Give it up for Seth Herzog.

00:06:05.998 --> 00:06:08.768
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:13.205 --> 00:06:15.742
[ "Wonder Woman" theme plays ]

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:23.315
-♪ Wonder Woman, Wonder Woman ♪

00:06:23.315 --> 00:06:27.119
-♪ All our hopes
are pinned upon you ♪

00:06:27.119 --> 00:06:31.157
-♪ And the magic that you do ♪

00:06:31.157 --> 00:06:34.794
♪ Stop a bullet cold
and make the axis fold ♪

00:06:34.794 --> 00:06:36.762
♪ Change their minds ♪

00:06:36.762 --> 00:06:42.301
♪ And change the world ♪

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:46.538
♪ Wonder Woman ♪

00:06:46.538 --> 00:06:49.308
♪ Wonder Woman ♪

00:06:49.308 --> 00:06:53.079
♪ You're a wonder,
Wonder Woman ♪

00:06:55.648 --> 00:06:58.283
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:58.283 --> 00:07:00.753
-Give it up for
Seth Herzog, everybody!

00:07:00.753 --> 00:07:03.656
Let's hear it for Gal Gadot!

00:07:03.656 --> 00:07:06.525
Once again "Wonder Woman"
and "Wonder Woman" meet.

00:07:06.525 --> 00:07:08.627
We'll be right back
with Barry Manilow.

00:07:08.627 --> 00:07:10.696
You cannot unsee that.

00:07:10.696 --> 00:07:13.866
♪♪

